  "finding": "All 57 late Bell VI samples in the current renderer show SP running and RDP pipe/command busy. CPU is outside user hooks in 53 samples and in board submission in 4; none samples gameplay update or UI. Average gameplay update is 0.617 ms versus 4.778 ms board submission and 1.382 ms UI. Rendering/queue completion is the main observed pressure.",
  "limitations": [
    "Read-only coarse VI status samples do not isolate RSP cost from RDP work, measure complete GPU time, or prove earlier mutation spikes irrelevant. SP not halted is not a count of useful instructions. Engine phase includes waits and engine work.",
    "CPU submission spans include asynchronous queue backpressure. Lower local ground-command time cannot be claimed as total-frame savings.",
    "Emulator-only, base 4 MiB, same legal native review input and unchanged tests/thresholds. No hardware FPS claim. Nominal FPS uses 60 VIs/s; real native VI clock is approximately 59.826 Hz.",
    "Additional review observation can slightly perturb cycle/buffer phase. Two fewer four-VI holds do not establish a material presentation improvement."
  ],
